1
00:01:18,519 --> 00:01:19,959
Right, just look at the camera.

2
00:01:20,319 --> 00:01:22,000
My name is Qian Yichuan.

3
00:01:23,159 --> 00:01:24,159
The "Yi" of chivalry and honor,

4
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,040
and "Chuan" for rivers flowing to the sea.

5
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:29,079
I'm...

6
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,400
an accountant in the finance department.

7
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:33,159
That's all.

8
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:35,879
I hear you're a college graduate.

9
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:36,680
That's right.

10
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,079
Graduated from the Business University.

11
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:39,640
Why come to Lapi Brewery?

12
00:01:40,359 --> 00:01:41,599
Why wouldn't I come to Lapi Brewery?

13
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:45,359
My father

14
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,079
worked at Lapi Brewery, too.

15
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,079
He was a factory worker.

16
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,680
He got sick and died during my senior year.

17
00:01:54,879 --> 00:01:55,680
After that,

18
00:01:56,959 --> 00:01:58,400
it was the factory uncles and elders

19
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:01,280
who pooled money to put me through college.

20
00:02:02,959 --> 00:02:04,120
I'm a child of Lapi.

21
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:05,959
After graduating,

22
00:02:06,319 --> 00:02:08,039
I had to return to Lapi and do my part.

23
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:10,000
I have a dream.

24
00:02:12,319 --> 00:02:13,360
I hope that one day,

25
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,319
people all around the world

26
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,639
will get to drink our Lapi beer.

27
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,599
That's great.

28
00:02:20,159 --> 00:02:20,840
Thank you.

29
00:02:23,479 --> 00:02:24,759
Your glasses have a bit of glare.

30
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:25,639
My glasses?

31
00:02:25,639 --> 00:02:26,680
This is Tu from our finance department.

32
00:02:26,719 --> 00:02:27,759
Why don't you interview her?

33
00:02:27,759 --> 00:02:28,800
Drink some water and shut it, will you?

34
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:30,360
You're so annoying.

35
00:02:30,919 --> 00:02:31,560
Say a few words!

36
00:02:31,639 --> 00:02:32,400
Chunyan, say a few words.

37
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,280
It's not an interview. Just say something.

38
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,680
Weren't you interviewing the college grad?

39
00:02:35,159 --> 00:02:36,039
What's your dream?

40
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:40,960
My dream is...

41
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:43,159
to get into college in my next life,

42
00:02:43,759 --> 00:02:44,919
just like Qian Yichuan.

43
00:02:47,599 --> 00:02:48,120
I...

44
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,960
I hope to have what it takes to be chief,

45
00:02:52,479 --> 00:02:53,520
and manage our factory well.

46
00:02:53,919 --> 00:02:55,159
Those last two lines were his dream,

47
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,199
not mine.

48
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:58,479
Didn't you say

49
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,080
you wanted to be the top dog in finance?

50
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,719
Stop talking about me!

51
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:39,839
This thing's pretty amazing.

52
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,040
Gotta admit, it works.

53
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:41,800
How so?

54
00:04:42,519 --> 00:04:44,000
If it worked, would I be lying here?

55
00:04:45,079 --> 00:04:46,040
How didn't it work?

56
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,199
Those other guys are all dead,

57
00:04:47,199 --> 00:04:48,000
and you're still breathing.

58
00:04:48,199 --> 00:04:49,000
Get it?

59
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,519
You're grinning like an idiot.

60
00:05:00,439 --> 00:05:01,279
I came to visit you.

61
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,800
Get me a jar of canned yellow peaches.

62
00:05:17,759 --> 00:05:18,399
A small jar, okay?

63
00:05:18,399 --> 00:05:19,160
I can't finish a big one.

64
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,279
How are you feeling?

65
00:05:38,079 --> 00:05:38,959
What's this?

66
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,360
Got the word

67
00:05:42,079 --> 00:05:43,079
and came to mourn me?

68
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,160
I'm alright.

69
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,279
Still alive.

70
00:05:46,399 --> 00:05:46,959
Not dead yet.

71
00:05:50,759 --> 00:05:51,480
Old Qian.

72
00:05:53,199 --> 00:05:54,759
I've always owed you an apology.

73
00:06:00,519 --> 00:06:02,040
All these years, I've kept having dreams.

74
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:03,639
Dreaming of

75
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,759
the days when I first came to the factory.

76
00:06:07,199 --> 00:06:08,920
The director asked what I wanted to film.

77
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,360
I said,

78
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:13,000
I wanted to film everyone's smiles.

79
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:16,959
Genuine smiles.

80
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:31,920
Back then,

81
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,639
I was just

82
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,639
a young reporter aiming for the truth.

83
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:41,720
You were

84
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:44,199
an accountant trying to make your mark

85
00:06:44,199 --> 00:06:45,319
at Lacheng's First State Factory.

86
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,000
We both uncovered a terrifying reality,

87
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:52,079
one far beyond our control.

88
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,759
But we both took the plunge anyway.

89
00:06:56,639 --> 00:06:57,360
So

90
00:06:58,360 --> 00:06:59,480
we're the same kind of person.

91
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,519
Maybe back then, who knows?

92
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,279
But right now,

93
00:07:10,279 --> 00:07:11,920
you're a big director in Beijing,

94
00:07:14,279 --> 00:07:16,319
and I'm just a watchdog in the factory.

95
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,279
To tell you the truth,

96
00:07:24,079 --> 00:07:25,600
I haven't had it easy out there.

97
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,560
It might look glamorous to outsiders,

98
00:07:29,519 --> 00:07:30,360
but it's all an illusion.

99
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,920
When I first left,

100
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:36,000
I was full of hope and big dreams.

101
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:38,759
I wanted to join the biggest network

102
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:40,560
as an investigative journalist.

103
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,600
But after all these years,

104
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,240
I couldn't even get into that department.

105
00:07:48,399 --> 00:07:49,680
Bouncing from one show to another,

106
00:07:50,399 --> 00:07:51,759
doing odd, menial jobs.

107
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,160
Finally scraped together some cash

108
00:07:56,199 --> 00:07:56,959
to make a film,

109
00:07:57,399 --> 00:07:58,480
only to end up buried in debt.

110
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,480
Honestly,

111
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,959
I've given up on those dreams.

112
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,839
Coming back this time, I just wanted

113
00:08:13,959 --> 00:08:15,240
to sell my place here,

114
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,079
pay off the bulk of my debts,

115
00:08:17,759 --> 00:08:18,959
quit journalism for good,

116
00:08:19,439 --> 00:08:20,279
find any random job

117
00:08:20,279 --> 00:08:21,160
just to get by,

118
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,240
and call it a life.

119
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,720
I don't know

120
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:30,279
what these years were all for,

121
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:32,960
nor do I know

122
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,639
what my future holds.

123
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:37,639
Just like you,

124
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:39,799
I'm completely lost.

125
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,240
Don't drag me into this.

126
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,600
I'm not lost at all.

127
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:49,759
What's your deal, anyway?

128
00:08:49,799 --> 00:08:50,480
Standing there today,

129
00:08:50,519 --> 00:08:51,679
rattling on and on—

130
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,000
did you come here to see who has it worse?

131
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:11,360
Sure.

132
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,600
Come on, let's go again.

133
00:09:15,159 --> 00:09:15,759
Get out, quick.

134
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:22,559
Where are you going?

135
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:23,480
Yan'er, come outside with me.

136
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:24,399
What for?

137
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:25,559
Just come outside with me.

138
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:26,879
Go on out.

139
00:09:27,519 --> 00:09:28,840
The men are talking. Why are you here?

140
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:31,080
Don't drag me!

141
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,919
It's fine. Don't worry.

142
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:36,720
Qian Yichuan.

143
00:09:37,799 --> 00:09:39,519
Heard you're scheming behind our backs.

144
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:42,840
Failed to win the factory at the auction,

145
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:43,480
and what?

146
00:09:43,639 --> 00:09:44,399
Can't accept it?

147
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,080
Of course I can't.

148
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,120
What's there not to accept?

149
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:49,240
The state's Restructuring this time

150
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:50,799
wasn't meant to abandon us

151
00:09:50,799 --> 00:09:51,919
and leave us to fend for ourselves.

152
00:09:52,879 --> 00:09:54,320
It's to motivate all of us

153
00:09:54,679 --> 00:09:55,840
to seek a better future.

154
00:09:58,360 --> 00:09:59,399
What do you call a better future?

155
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,120
Do you need someone who loves the factory,

156
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,080
has real management skills,

157
00:10:03,159 --> 00:10:04,879
and can bring everyone together,

158
00:10:05,279 --> 00:10:05,840
or do you want someone

159
00:10:05,879 --> 00:10:07,600
who abuses power and breaks the law?

160
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:08,879
What's going on?

161
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,879
Why did you bring so many people?

162
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,200
Leizi.

163
00:10:16,799 --> 00:10:18,080
We grew up together.

164
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,120
Inside this factory yard,

165
00:10:21,039 --> 00:10:21,799
playing marbles,

166
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,399
playing hide-and-seek.

167
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:25,320
Tell me,

168
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,519
all our relatives and neighbors here,

169
00:10:27,879 --> 00:10:29,039
aren't they all workers of this factory?

170
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:31,840
Don't you love this factory?

171
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,080
I do.

172
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:37,320
Don't you want this factory to thrive?

173
00:10:39,919 --> 00:10:40,960
I do.

174
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,720
It's just like choosing a parent.

175
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,720
If we pick the wrong parent,

176
00:10:49,519 --> 00:10:50,720
we'll end up like orphans,

177
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,120
starving and freezing to death.

178
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,480
Am I wrong?

179
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,720
You sure can run your mouth.

180
00:11:07,279 --> 00:11:08,679
I only heard about it before,

181
00:11:10,279 --> 00:11:11,519
but today I heard it myself.

182
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:13,679
Saw it with my own eyes.

183
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,559
You think you know it all, Qian Yichuan?

184
00:11:18,679 --> 00:11:20,639
Duped those who didn't know better, huh?

185
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,639
Confusing those who actually did.

186
00:11:28,799 --> 00:11:30,039
I'm asking you just one thing today.

187
00:11:30,919 --> 00:11:31,600
From now on,

188
00:11:32,519 --> 00:11:33,600
can you keep that foul mouth shut?

189
00:11:33,639 --> 00:11:34,639
No.

190
00:11:40,519 --> 00:11:41,960
Are you begging for a beating?

191
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:44,000
What would you do with this factory?

192
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:45,840
If given the chance,

193
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,159
I'd make a great manager.

194
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:51,559
Give you an inch, and you take a mile!

195
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,720
Just give me your word right now:

196
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,679
all that crap you spewed was bullshit,

197
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,200
and you were just talking drunk.

198
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,000
You're full of shit!

199
00:12:03,279 --> 00:12:04,000
So you want to do this the hard way!

200
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,200
I'm the one cutting you some slack here!

201
00:12:05,759 --> 00:12:06,840
Listen up, all of you!

202
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:07,679
Let me tell you,

203
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:09,480
I have all the evidence

204
00:12:09,559 --> 00:12:10,960
of Ma Guowen's crimes in my hands!

205
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,639
The moment I hand this over,

206
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,720
not just Ma Guowen,

207
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:16,879
but every single one of you lapdogs,

208
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,399
none of you will get away!

209
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,080
Get him!

210
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:19,799
Screw you!

211
00:12:21,879 --> 00:12:22,480
Beat him!

212
00:12:27,879 --> 00:12:28,600
Get off me!

213
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,360
Stop!

214
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,200
Keep hitting him!

215
00:12:47,879 --> 00:12:48,360
Leizi!

216
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,840
Leizi, darn you!

217
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:50,679
Touch him again...

218
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:51,559
Get lost!

219
00:13:04,039 --> 00:13:04,759
It's okay now.

220
00:13:08,559 --> 00:13:09,159
Let's go.

221
00:13:21,639 --> 00:13:22,840
Iron Crutch Li

222
00:13:24,279 --> 00:13:25,440
Clubfoot Seven

223
00:13:26,879 --> 00:13:28,080
Crippled Foot

224
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,279
Cripple Qian

225
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,320
Anyway, from that day on,

226
00:13:34,559 --> 00:13:35,919
no one called me Qian Yichuan anymore.

227
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,200
But at least that day...

228
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,559
I didn't bow my head.

229
00:13:56,279 --> 00:13:56,919
Old Qian...

230
00:13:58,799 --> 00:13:59,559
I respect you.

231
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,440
If it were me,

232
00:14:05,559 --> 00:14:06,639
I don't know how I'd have ended up.

233
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,200
What's the matter?

234
00:14:21,679 --> 00:14:22,960
Actually tearing up?

235
00:14:25,919 --> 00:14:27,399
What are you crying for?

236
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:29,960
Even in my condition, I'm hanging tough.

237
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,399
You... you've got all your limbs.

238
00:14:31,399 --> 00:14:32,639
What are you crying over there for?

239
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,799
If you're out of money, just earn more.

240
00:14:35,799 --> 00:14:37,159
Money is nothing, let me tell you.

241
00:14:38,519 --> 00:14:40,159
Keeping your chin up is what matters most.

242
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,399
You've gotta keep your spirits up.

243
00:14:41,519 --> 00:14:42,960
A person needs some backbone, you know?

244
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,399
Chunyan and I are heading to Sanya soon.

245
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:50,639
Go swimming.

246
00:14:50,759 --> 00:14:51,480
Soak up the sun.

247
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:53,679
Right?

248
00:14:56,759 --> 00:14:57,440
So goodbye,

249
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:00,559
and never see you again.

250
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,039
Goodbye

251
00:15:33,919 --> 00:15:34,600
Oh, man!

252
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:35,759
Looking so handsome!

253
00:15:36,159 --> 00:15:36,720
Sharp!

254
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,080
You happy with it?

255
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,399
How could I not be?

256
00:15:40,559 --> 00:15:41,440
Love it!

257
00:15:41,559 --> 00:15:42,759
With this haircut,

258
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:45,720
do I look like an accountant?

259
00:15:49,559 --> 00:15:50,159
All set.

260
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:51,080
All done.

261
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,159
How much is it?

262
00:15:52,559 --> 00:15:53,080
Twenty.

263
00:15:53,559 --> 00:15:54,960
No discount, buddy?

264
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:56,159
Call it 15.

265
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,200
Great!

266
00:15:57,279 --> 00:15:58,080
Fifteen, exact change.

267
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:58,639
Thank you!

268
00:15:58,759 --> 00:15:59,360
You're welcome.

269
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,000
Come on.

270
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,000
I want to go somewhere...

271
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:04,799
...to say goodbye.

272
00:16:07,279 --> 00:16:08,000
Where to?

273
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,120
Guess.

274
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:13,600
Don't tell me it's where we first—

275
00:16:15,919 --> 00:16:16,679
What are you doing?

276
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:17,720
People are watching!

277
00:16:17,879 --> 00:16:18,759
What's there to be afraid of?

278
00:16:18,759 --> 00:16:19,720
Who hasn't been in love?

279
00:16:19,879 --> 00:16:21,080
Doesn't the barber date too?

280
00:16:21,639 --> 00:16:22,279
Are we a good match?

281
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:22,919
A great match.

282
00:16:23,919 --> 00:16:25,200
All right, put it on.

283
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:27,759
Let's go.

284
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:29,519
Your hair!

285
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:33,600
Let's go.

286
00:16:33,799 --> 00:16:34,200
Come on.

287
00:16:34,559 --> 00:16:35,320
Hold onto me.

288
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:35,799
Holding on, holding on.

289
00:16:35,799 --> 00:16:36,279
Holding you tight.

290
00:16:38,799 --> 00:16:40,600
Liu Xuemei's son is named Liu Xiaosheng.

291
00:16:41,399 --> 00:16:42,200
He works in broadband.

292
00:16:42,879 --> 00:16:44,159
He's right in Lacheng.

293
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:45,759
I managed to get his phone number.

294
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,320
I'll send it to your WeChat in a bit.

295
00:16:49,519 --> 00:16:50,320
Contact him.

296
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:51,840
Be sure to meet with him.

297
00:16:52,399 --> 00:16:53,440
No problem, I'll get in touch.

298
00:16:55,919 --> 00:16:57,720
No idea what Sister Miao caught wind of,

299
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:58,639
but she keeps asking around.

300
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:00,799
She says...

301
00:17:01,279 --> 00:17:03,000
if you're willing to work with her,

302
00:17:03,679 --> 00:17:05,000
you can name your price.

303
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,319
I have no intention of working with her.

304
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,079
Don't tell her a thing.

305
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,720
I wouldn't dare without your say-so.

306
00:17:14,799 --> 00:17:16,119
If we're going to do this,

307
00:17:16,799 --> 00:17:18,880
we need to find someone reliable,

308
00:17:19,559 --> 00:17:20,799
a credible organization.

309
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:24,160
Reliable and credible...

310
00:17:24,359 --> 00:17:25,200
Going with a TV station

311
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,200
might be more dependable.

312
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:28,880
Only thing is,

313
00:17:29,559 --> 00:17:30,119
the money...

314
00:17:30,119 --> 00:17:31,480
won't be as much as public accounts pay.

315
00:17:32,319 --> 00:17:34,119
I never planned on making money off this.

316
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:37,240
Much respect.

317
00:17:37,759 --> 00:17:38,160
Cheers to you.

318
00:17:41,079 --> 00:17:41,839
I've got a lot to learn from you.

319
00:17:43,119 --> 00:17:44,160
I can't quite remember it.

320
00:17:45,039 --> 00:17:46,480
The first line went something like...

321
00:17:46,799 --> 00:17:47,440
I know!

322
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:50,000
"Thugs in the pool hall picked a fight,"

323
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:50,359
Right.

324
00:17:51,039 --> 00:17:52,640
"Left poor Chuanzi in a daze."

325
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:55,480
"Tu Chunyan flew in through the air,"

326
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,880
"And knocked down the whole damn bunch!"

327
00:17:58,839 --> 00:18:01,359
What, want me to get you glasses tomorrow?

328
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:02,680
This door...

329
00:18:03,599 --> 00:18:04,720
I could open it with my eyes closed.

330
00:18:07,799 --> 00:18:09,519
Opened it with your eyes closed indeed!

331
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,079
Let's go.

332
00:18:19,559 --> 00:18:20,640
What were you thinking,

333
00:18:20,759 --> 00:18:22,359
insisting on visiting the factory again?

334
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:23,640
I'm leaving soon.

335
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,039
Not sure if I'll ever come back.

336
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,319
Just want to take a look,

337
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:27,799
for old times' sake.

338
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,960
Leave it to an educated guy like you.

339
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,079
I'll send Liu Xiaosheng's number

340
00:18:37,079 --> 00:18:38,160
to your phone.

341
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:40,240
Hello?

342
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:40,960
Hello?

343
00:18:42,559 --> 00:18:43,279
Leshui?

344
00:18:44,319 --> 00:18:45,039
It's Qian Yichuan.

345
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:47,079
Old Qian.

346
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:48,599
Are you free?

347
00:18:48,599 --> 00:18:49,680
I want to talk to you about the case.

348
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,240
Sure.

349
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,640
Where should I meet you?

350
00:18:53,079 --> 00:18:53,880
I'm at the old factory.

351
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:54,839
Let's meet at the gate soon.

352
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:56,240
How long will it take?

353
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:57,680
I'm heading over right now.

354
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:58,440
Wait for me.

355
00:18:58,880 --> 00:18:59,400
All right.

356
00:19:00,039 --> 00:19:01,039
Chunyan and I

357
00:19:01,039 --> 00:19:03,960
will stroll up to the malt silo first.

358
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:04,960
Talk to you when you get here.

359
00:19:05,119 --> 00:19:05,799
Call me.

360
00:19:06,319 --> 00:19:06,759
Will do.

361
00:19:13,839 --> 00:19:15,519
Haven't been up there in ages.

362
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,599
Still pretty nimble on your feet!

363
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:34,839
Not bad.

364
00:19:35,079 --> 00:19:35,759
Take it slow, it's slippery.

365
00:19:35,759 --> 00:19:36,240
Here.

366
00:19:37,039 --> 00:19:39,039
Easy does it, Master Qian.

367
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:40,640
Man...

368
00:19:42,319 --> 00:19:43,200
I think you're...

369
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:44,200
doing pretty well.

370
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,200
Haven't been up here in ages.

371
00:19:49,359 --> 00:19:50,240
Now that we're up here...

372
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:51,000
it hits me...

373
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,759
just how huge our factory really is.

374
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,640
Yeah.

375
00:19:59,039 --> 00:19:59,839
It's huge...

376
00:20:00,799 --> 00:20:01,519
and old.

377
00:20:03,319 --> 00:20:04,119
A lot of people spend their whole lives...

378
00:20:04,119 --> 00:20:05,640
without ever leaving this place.

379
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:15,880
Don't talk nonsense.

380
00:20:16,039 --> 00:20:17,599
Remember the first time we came up here?

381
00:20:20,119 --> 00:20:20,799
Don't bring that up.

382
00:20:20,799 --> 00:20:22,640
You told me, "Qian Yichuan, I'm cold."

383
00:20:23,359 --> 00:20:24,960
La-la-la, I'm not listening!

384
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,759
So I took off my coat and gave it to you.

385
00:20:27,519 --> 00:20:29,240
You said, "Qian Yichuan, I'm still cold."

386
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,160
You're so annoying!

387
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:31,640
So I took off my shirt for you too.

388
00:20:33,079 --> 00:20:34,759
You said, "Qian Yichuan, my legs are cold."

389
00:20:35,279 --> 00:20:36,119
Shut up already!

390
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:04,720
Qian Yichuan.

391
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:05,759
Hello,

392
00:21:06,279 --> 00:21:08,400
the number you dialed is powered off.

393
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,160
Sorry.

394
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,079
Officer Han,

395
00:21:28,759 --> 00:21:30,440
Qian Yichuan wanted to see me.

396
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:32,319
He asked to meet by the old factory gate.

397
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:34,079
I'm here right now,

398
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,440
but I don't see him.

399
00:21:36,319 --> 00:21:37,319
His phone isn't going through either.

400
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:38,559
How could you go out this late,

401
00:21:38,559 --> 00:21:40,279
all alone to such a dangerous place?

402
00:21:40,279 --> 00:21:41,599
Get out of there right now!

403
00:21:42,319 --> 00:21:43,680
He said it's related to the case.

404
00:21:44,079 --> 00:21:45,880
No matter what, you shouldn't have gone!

405
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:47,640
That old factory is so dangerous!

406
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:48,880
Leave right now.

407
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,720
Go home.

408
00:21:50,079 --> 00:21:51,799
Text me when you get home, okay?

409
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,079
I'll head over in a bit.

410
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,119
I'll help you look for him.

411
00:21:54,119 --> 00:21:54,599
All right?

412
00:21:54,599 --> 00:21:55,880
I'll call you once I find him.

413
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:56,759
Don't worry.

414
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:58,319
Okay.

415
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:06,559
Let's head over to the old factory.

416
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:07,759
You two come with me.

417
00:22:08,079 --> 00:22:08,480
Let's move.

418
00:22:31,839 --> 00:22:32,359
Hello?

419
00:22:33,119 --> 00:22:33,799
Shen Leshui.

420
00:22:34,319 --> 00:22:35,000
Where are you?

421
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:36,400
I'm in the car.

422
00:22:36,599 --> 00:22:37,640
Didn't you tell me to head back?

423
00:22:38,279 --> 00:22:38,880
Good, head home.

424
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:41,400
My men and I are at the old factory gate.

425
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:42,759
Then I'll come meet you.

426
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:43,759
Don't come back.

427
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:46,279
I'll go track down Qian Yichuan.

428
00:22:55,039 --> 00:22:55,880
You two go right.

429
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:57,279
I'll take the front.

430
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:57,799
Okay.

431
00:22:57,799 --> 00:22:59,240
Report anything immediately.

432
00:22:59,400 --> 00:22:59,920
Copy that.

433
00:23:00,079 --> 00:23:00,799
Stay safe.

434
00:23:00,799 --> 00:23:01,240
Let's move.

435
00:23:01,759 --> 00:23:02,240
Driver,

436
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,839
turn around and head back.

437
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:40,119
Xiao Wu, Wenxiu.

438
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:41,319
Copy that, copy that.

439
00:23:42,279 --> 00:23:43,680
By the malt silo in the old factory,

440
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,200
there's been a murder.

441
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:46,680
Requesting backup.

442
00:23:46,799 --> 00:23:47,279
Copy that.

443
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:58,440
Who is it?

444
00:24:58,680 --> 00:24:59,359
Qian Yichuan.

445
00:25:21,319 --> 00:25:21,799
Chuang!

446
00:25:22,079 --> 00:25:23,160
We're at the bottom of the malt silo!

447
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,000
At the bottom of the malt silo, Chuang!

448
00:25:24,079 --> 00:25:24,599
Where are you?

449
00:25:24,599 --> 00:25:25,200
Chuang, over there!

450
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:25,799
Where are you?

451
00:25:25,839 --> 00:25:26,279
Over there!

452
00:25:26,279 --> 00:25:26,920
Hey, Chuang!

453
00:25:27,319 --> 00:25:27,960
Hey, Chuang!

454
00:25:28,759 --> 00:25:29,640
Xiao Wu, wait here.

455
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:29,960
Okay.

456
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:32,720
Hey, Chuang!

457
00:25:32,799 --> 00:25:33,640
Hey, Chuang!

458
00:25:34,119 --> 00:25:34,880
Chuang!

459
00:25:35,119 --> 00:25:35,680
Chuang!

460
00:25:39,759 --> 00:25:40,400
Chuang!

461
00:26:13,279 --> 00:26:14,000
Xiao Wu.

462
00:26:16,079 --> 00:26:16,680
Where's Chuang?

463
00:26:17,079 --> 00:26:17,599
Over there.

464
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:18,599
Xiao Gao.

465
00:26:18,839 --> 00:26:19,599
Chuang's over here!

466
00:26:19,599 --> 00:26:20,119
What's the situation?

467
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:21,680
Someone fell from up high over there.

468
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:22,839
No vital signs.

469
00:26:23,079 --> 00:26:24,240
A black plastic bag is over the head.

470
00:26:26,759 --> 00:26:27,319
Chuang!

471
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:30,440
What happened to him?

472
00:26:30,440 --> 00:26:31,160
Is that Han Chuang?

473
00:26:32,079 --> 00:26:32,720
Captain Cheng!

474
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:34,680
Where are the medics?

475
00:26:34,839 --> 00:26:35,680
An officer is injured!

476
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:36,319
Hurry!

477
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:38,440
Get him to the hospital, now!

478
00:26:38,519 --> 00:26:39,359
Cai Wenxiu, go with him.

479
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:40,759
Report back to me with any updates.

480
00:26:41,119 --> 00:26:41,599
Got it. Hurry!

481
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:46,960
The scene is cordoned off.

482
00:26:47,039 --> 00:26:47,839
Investigation is underway.

483
00:26:51,920 --> 00:26:52,839
Lock down the crime scene!

484
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:53,319
Yes, sir!

485
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:57,559
Captain Cheng.

486
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,640
Chuang's heading to the hospital.

487
00:27:01,960 --> 00:27:03,119
Calling Captain Cheng! Calling Captain Cheng!

488
00:27:03,759 --> 00:27:05,000
Found a woman on top of the silo!

489
00:27:05,119 --> 00:27:06,000
She has vital signs!

490
00:27:08,559 --> 00:27:09,079
Keep watch down here.

491
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:10,119
I'm going up to check.

492
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:10,920
Let's go.

493
00:27:28,839 --> 00:27:29,240
Gao.

494
00:27:29,319 --> 00:27:30,440
While searching the scene,

495
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:31,160
we found this person.

496
00:27:37,359 --> 00:27:38,160
What are you doing here?

497
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,599
I'm the one who called Officer Han.

498
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,079
Where is he?

499
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:46,200
What did you say?

500
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:50,319
I called Officer Han.

501
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:53,559
You called him?

502
00:27:58,640 --> 00:27:59,240
She can't leave.

503
00:28:00,319 --> 00:28:02,079
Track her movements.

504
00:28:02,200 --> 00:28:03,680
Check her chat history.

505
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:04,480
Call logs.

506
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:06,400
And the card in her camera.

507
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:08,200
Take it out and check every single second!

508
00:28:08,799 --> 00:28:09,440
Give me the camera.

509
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:11,880
Hand it over!

510
00:28:30,640 --> 00:28:31,880
Doctor, how is he doing?

511
00:28:32,079 --> 00:28:33,200
He's not out of danger yet.

512
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:34,079
He's still under observation.

513
00:28:35,559 --> 00:28:37,599
Is his life in any danger?

514
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,480
Don't panic. Just wait a little longer.

515
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:40,200
Roughly how long?

516
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:42,279
It's hard to say.

517
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:46,720
Please do everything you can.

518
00:29:02,799 --> 00:29:03,279
Hello?

519
00:29:04,759 --> 00:29:05,319
Go ahead.

520
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:06,920
We have to wait a few more hours...

521
00:29:07,039 --> 00:29:08,400
...to know if she'll be okay.

522
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:09,839
How are things on your end?

523
00:29:11,799 --> 00:29:12,279
All right.

524
00:29:13,319 --> 00:29:14,880
Tell me right away if anything comes up.

525
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:15,640
I'll head right over.

526
00:29:16,160 --> 00:29:16,640
Appreciate it.

527
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:17,680
Bye.

528
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:20,799
How's Tu Chunyan?

529
00:29:23,119 --> 00:29:24,160
How is she?

530
00:29:24,839 --> 00:29:26,319
How is Tu Chunyan?

531
00:29:31,079 --> 00:29:31,960
No comment.

532
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:17,400
Wh-Who are you?

533
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:18,440
Wait a second!

534
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:18,920
The director isn't in!

535
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:19,880
What are you doing?

536
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:21,400
The director isn't here!

537
00:30:21,759 --> 00:30:22,200
Director!

538
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:23,279
Well, isn't this Chunyan?

539
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:24,279
It's fine. Head on out.

540
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:25,359
What's going on here?

541
00:30:25,640 --> 00:30:26,359
Good grief!

542
00:30:26,559 --> 00:30:28,319
Qian Yichuan got beaten up!

543
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:30,960
Th-That really happened?

544
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:31,559
Never mind that.

545
00:30:31,559 --> 00:30:32,160
Was it...

546
00:30:32,319 --> 00:30:32,960
the Security Section?

547
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:33,920
It was them, wasn't it?

548
00:30:34,440 --> 00:30:36,000
Security Section? The Security Section?

549
00:30:37,279 --> 00:30:38,240
Oh, my god!

550
00:30:38,319 --> 00:30:39,839
There's even blood everywhere!

551
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:42,759
Is he all right?

552
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:45,000
Look at your face, covered in blood!

553
00:30:45,119 --> 00:30:46,400
What on earth happened?

554
00:30:46,799 --> 00:30:47,759
Where is he? Where's he at?

555
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,240
Stop playing dumb!

556
00:30:49,839 --> 00:30:51,359
You set those thugs on him!

557
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:53,079
It's just the two of us in here.

558
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:54,799
Stop putting on an act for me!

559
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:55,559
Chunyan...

560
00:30:55,559 --> 00:30:56,880
Why are you talking so reckless?

561
00:30:57,279 --> 00:30:58,279
Look at you, such a pretty girl,

562
00:30:58,319 --> 00:30:59,079
with blood all over your face.

563
00:30:59,079 --> 00:30:59,519
It ruins your looks.

564
00:30:59,519 --> 00:30:59,960
Come here, come on.

565
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:00,680
Wipe it off, wipe it off.

566
00:31:01,839 --> 00:31:04,000
You must give me a straight answer today!

567
00:31:05,039 --> 00:31:05,680
Oh, boy...

568
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:07,079
You're gonna pay!

569
00:31:07,119 --> 00:31:08,960
You have to pay Qian's medical bills!

570
00:31:09,119 --> 00:31:10,519
Otherwise, I'm not leaving!

571
00:31:13,519 --> 00:31:14,079
Don't, don't, don't.

572
00:31:14,079 --> 00:31:14,839
Calm down, calm down.

573
00:31:14,839 --> 00:31:15,559
Let's talk this through slowly.

574
00:31:15,680 --> 00:31:16,160
All right?

575
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:17,759
Have some water.

576
00:31:20,839 --> 00:31:22,119
Look, about this factory...

577
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:23,480
I've been running it pretty well.

578
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:25,720
Then Qian Yichuan riled everyone up,

579
00:31:25,720 --> 00:31:27,720
and a whole crowd started making trouble.

580
00:31:28,079 --> 00:31:30,279
As if they'd suffered some huge injustice.

581
00:31:31,559 --> 00:31:33,559
I didn't do anything to cross them!

582
00:31:34,319 --> 00:31:34,720
Here, here, here.

583
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:35,279
Drink up, have some water.

584
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:39,240
Let me show you something.

585
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:40,240
Come, take a look at this.

586
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:45,279
This is the layoff list.

587
00:31:45,680 --> 00:31:46,640
Look closely.

588
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:47,319
Are you on it or not?

589
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:49,319
Are you on here?

590
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:53,079
Aren't you doing just fine?

591
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:54,440
I didn't get you laid off, did I?

592
00:32:00,279 --> 00:32:01,319
Hear me out.

593
00:32:02,079 --> 00:32:03,079
This Lapi Brewery...

594
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:04,160
is our home,

595
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:06,559
and everyone's gotta take care of it.

596
00:32:07,920 --> 00:32:08,880
The brewery's Restructuring,

597
00:32:09,519 --> 00:32:11,680
so some folks definitely gotta go.

598
00:32:12,279 --> 00:32:13,400
And as for the ones who leave,

599
00:32:13,599 --> 00:32:14,559
I never said I'd leave them hanging.

600
00:32:15,559 --> 00:32:17,079
Didn't we set up night training classes

601
00:32:17,119 --> 00:32:18,079
to teach everyone stuff like

602
00:32:18,759 --> 00:32:20,079
zipper repair,

603
00:32:20,519 --> 00:32:21,680
bike repair,

604
00:32:21,799 --> 00:32:22,839
and then massage,

605
00:32:22,839 --> 00:32:23,559
and foot baths?

606
00:32:23,839 --> 00:32:24,799
We've got all those classes, don't we?

607
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:27,000
Haven't I done enough?

608
00:32:28,400 --> 00:32:29,160
Chunyan,

609
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:31,480
you're such a good-looking girl,

610
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:33,400
and you're sharp as a tack.

611
00:32:33,599 --> 00:32:34,680
Just work hard here at the brewery.

612
00:32:34,720 --> 00:32:35,960
You've got a bright future ahead.

613
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:37,319
Why are you messing around

614
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:38,920
with that crowd?

615
00:32:39,880 --> 00:32:41,079
Why waste your time with that nonsense?

616
00:32:43,119 --> 00:32:44,480
You're not getting any younger.

617
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:48,119
Are you seeing

618
00:32:48,559 --> 00:32:49,680
Qian Yichuan, huh?

619
00:32:51,119 --> 00:32:52,440
That guy's no good.

620
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,759
At your age,

621
00:32:54,240 --> 00:32:55,759
it's easy to misjudge people,

622
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:56,519
you know?

623
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:57,559
He's a nobody.

624
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:59,440
If he ever becomes a boss someday,

625
00:33:00,440 --> 00:33:01,880
he definitely won't want you anymore.

626
00:33:01,880 --> 00:33:02,440
Got it?

627
00:33:02,960 --> 00:33:04,160
If he doesn't want you,

628
00:33:04,519 --> 00:33:05,640
I want you!

629
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:07,640
I want you.

630
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:11,119
Holy crap!

631
00:33:15,279 --> 00:33:16,119
You filthy pervert!

632
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:17,160
Ow, Jesus!

633
00:33:18,759 --> 00:33:19,640
You filthy pervert!

634
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:21,160
I'll kill you, you hear me?!

635
00:33:21,319 --> 00:33:21,960
I'll kill you!

636
00:33:22,839 --> 00:33:23,480
Ow, my God!

637
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:24,839
Holy crap!

638
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:27,240
That's enough! Cut it out!

639
00:33:27,400 --> 00:33:28,960
Believe me, I'll kill you!

640
00:33:29,440 --> 00:33:30,200
Ow, damn it!

641
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:31,240
Let me tell you,

642
00:33:31,359 --> 00:33:32,519
you're laid off, you hear me?!

643
00:33:32,519 --> 00:33:33,359
If you keep this up—

644
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:34,160
That's enough already!

645
00:33:34,279 --> 00:33:35,519
I'm not afraid of you!

646
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:38,079
Security! Security! Security!

647
00:33:38,559 --> 00:33:39,559
Security!

648
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:40,519
Security!

649
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:41,559
Drag her out of here!

650
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,480
You filthy pervert!

651
00:33:44,559 --> 00:33:45,319
Assaulting factory leadership!

652
00:33:45,319 --> 00:33:46,319
I'll kill you! You won't get away with this!

653
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,880
I'll kill you!

654
00:34:11,760 --> 00:34:12,719
Qian Yichuan!

655
00:34:14,199 --> 00:34:15,039
Qian Yichuan!

656
00:34:18,480 --> 00:34:19,239
Qian Yichuan!

657
00:34:20,880 --> 00:34:21,480
Oh, man.

658
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:23,519
I knew you'd be sitting by the river.

659
00:34:25,599 --> 00:34:27,000
Why are you looking so handsome today?

660
00:34:27,599 --> 00:34:28,440
You're not wearing glasses.

661
00:34:29,760 --> 00:34:30,920
Usually when you wear them,

662
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:31,719
blinking your eyes all the time,

663
00:34:31,760 --> 00:34:32,599
you don't look handsome at all.

664
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:34,000
You look better without them.

665
00:34:34,599 --> 00:34:36,079
You had those for so many years anyway.

666
00:34:36,079 --> 00:34:37,599
If they're broken, we'll buy a new pair.

667
00:34:39,679 --> 00:34:41,239
Look at the good food I brought you.

668
00:34:42,079 --> 00:34:42,719
You have it.

669
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:43,719
I'm not hungry.

670
00:34:44,320 --> 00:34:45,639
A buddy just treated me to barbecue.

671
00:34:49,079 --> 00:34:50,000
Scrambled eggs with tomatoes.

672
00:34:50,079 --> 00:34:50,880
It's really delicious.

673
00:34:53,599 --> 00:34:54,679
After catching up with you,

674
00:34:55,519 --> 00:34:57,079
I have to head over to the paper mill.

675
00:35:02,599 --> 00:35:03,639
What's your rush?

676
00:35:03,719 --> 00:35:05,000
Your leg hasn't fully healed yet.

677
00:35:05,199 --> 00:35:05,800
Take it easy.

678
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:07,719
I'm not in a rush,

679
00:35:09,079 --> 00:35:09,840
they are.

680
00:35:10,920 --> 00:35:12,320
So many good jobs are waiting for me,

681
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,480
I have to sift through them carefully.

682
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:19,760
How are you doing?

683
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:33,159
I'm doing just fine.

684
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:36,599
Plenty of jobs are fighting over me too.

685
00:35:37,239 --> 00:35:38,320
I'm in no rush.

686
00:35:38,840 --> 00:35:40,320
I've got to sift through them carefully

687
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:42,960
and pick one that pays well.

688
00:35:47,440 --> 00:35:48,679
Give me a break.

689
00:35:50,679 --> 00:35:52,639
I heard you on the phone with your aunt.

690
00:35:53,639 --> 00:35:55,320
Do you know how hard it is to find work?

691
00:35:55,719 --> 00:35:56,719
Nobody's hiring anywhere.

692
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:02,719
If they don't want me, fine.

693
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:03,599
Suits me fine.

694
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:05,559
Even tigers take naps,

695
00:36:05,559 --> 00:36:07,199
and even bears hibernate for the winter.

696
00:36:07,920 --> 00:36:09,599
Who works in the dead of winter anyway?

697
00:36:09,599 --> 00:36:10,840
I don't even want to go outside.

698
00:36:11,239 --> 00:36:11,880
It's the perfect time

699
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:12,800
to get some rest.

700
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,760
Once this winter passes,

701
00:36:15,880 --> 00:36:16,800
the snow melts,

702
00:36:16,840 --> 00:36:17,719
and it warms up,

703
00:36:18,239 --> 00:36:20,400
I'll go sell cracked corn porridge

704
00:36:20,519 --> 00:36:21,360
and tea eggs.

705
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:25,079
Cao Jun already set up a tea egg stand

706
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:26,760
and started selling them.

707
00:36:29,039 --> 00:36:30,119
I looked into it.

708
00:36:31,840 --> 00:36:34,320
You only make 9.5 cents per egg.

709
00:36:35,320 --> 00:36:36,320
That's less than a dime.

710
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:39,360
Can you even sell a hundred a day?

711
00:36:41,079 --> 00:36:42,480
Look around our factory.

712
00:36:43,079 --> 00:36:45,320
Five tea egg stalls every 100 meters.

713
00:36:47,280 --> 00:36:47,840
Besides,

714
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:51,000
I used to work in the admin office.

715
00:36:52,159 --> 00:36:53,079
How can I go compete

716
00:36:53,079 --> 00:36:54,480
with forklift drivers for business?

717
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:56,719
What's so special about the admin office?

718
00:36:58,079 --> 00:36:59,639
Don't you still have to make a living?

719
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:04,400
Look at you.

720
00:37:05,519 --> 00:37:06,119
The cushy jobs?

721
00:37:06,119 --> 00:37:06,960
Nobody's offering them to you.

722
00:37:07,599 --> 00:37:08,239
Heavy labor?

723
00:37:08,239 --> 00:37:09,159
You can't handle that either.

724
00:37:10,159 --> 00:37:10,960
What's wrong with you?

725
00:37:12,559 --> 00:37:13,920
Look at the situation we're in.

726
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,599
You still can't let go of your pride.

727
00:37:24,400 --> 00:37:25,360
How about this?

728
00:37:26,679 --> 00:37:27,320
Why don't

729
00:37:28,639 --> 00:37:29,920
we head down south?

730
00:37:31,119 --> 00:37:33,800
It's freezing here with all this snow.

731
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:35,159
We'll go down south,

732
00:37:35,639 --> 00:37:36,880
face the ocean,

733
00:37:37,480 --> 00:37:38,760
and enjoy the warm spring.

734
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:41,320
We can hustle and start a small business.

735
00:37:41,719 --> 00:37:43,960
Who knows, we might become big bosses

736
00:37:44,239 --> 00:37:45,320
and get rich.

737
00:37:45,719 --> 00:37:46,440
Right, Boss Qian?

738
00:37:47,079 --> 00:37:47,800
I'll just latch onto you then.

739
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:48,519
I'll live off a big shot.

740
00:37:48,559 --> 00:37:49,960
Boss Qian, Boss Qian, Boss Qian!

741
00:37:54,159 --> 00:37:55,320
Oh man, it's freezing!

742
00:37:56,199 --> 00:37:57,599
Why is it so cold this winter?

743
00:38:17,519 --> 00:38:18,199
What are you doing?

744
00:38:29,639 --> 00:38:30,760
I have a bachelor's degree.

745
00:38:32,119 --> 00:38:32,880
What about you?

746
00:38:35,400 --> 00:38:36,199
Vocational school, right?

747
00:38:38,280 --> 00:38:39,079
I

748
00:38:39,880 --> 00:38:41,199
can recite pi

749
00:38:41,239 --> 00:38:42,639
to 270 decimal places.

750
00:38:43,159 --> 00:38:43,800
And you?

751
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:46,400
You can barely flick an abacus.

752
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,039
What are you getting at?

753
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:52,800
What am I getting at?

754
00:38:55,119 --> 00:38:56,079
What I'm saying is,

755
00:38:58,199 --> 00:38:59,440
I don't think we're a match.

756
00:39:06,239 --> 00:39:07,960
So let's not waste each other's time.

757
00:39:11,840 --> 00:39:12,400
That's it.

758
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:54,559
Xiao Tu.

759
00:39:56,679 --> 00:39:57,519
What are you doing here?

760
00:40:02,519 --> 00:40:03,800
Who upset you this time?

761
00:40:07,320 --> 00:40:07,760
Here...

762
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:09,000
Have a candied hawthorn.

763
00:40:09,559 --> 00:40:11,079
Something sweet will make it all pass.

764
00:40:11,239 --> 00:40:11,880
Everything'll be fine.

765
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:13,840
Take it.

766
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:24,440
It's filthy. It got so dirty.

767
00:40:24,559 --> 00:40:25,440
Can't eat it now.

768
00:40:27,639 --> 00:40:29,280
Anyway, I traded leftover tea eggs

769
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:30,360
with the vendor for it.

770
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:33,159
I'll buy you a fresh one tomorrow.

771
00:40:39,119 --> 00:40:40,519
I know you're hurting inside.

772
00:40:45,519 --> 00:40:47,079
With Old Qian's leg like this,

773
00:40:47,599 --> 00:40:48,599
who could feel good about that?

774
00:40:51,599 --> 00:40:52,760
But you've got to have hope.

775
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:54,880
His leg will definitely get better.

776
00:40:56,119 --> 00:40:56,920
Take me, for example.

777
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:59,320
I knew nothing besides driving a forklift.

778
00:40:59,599 --> 00:41:00,920
Now I sell tea eggs

779
00:41:01,320 --> 00:41:02,480
and do deliveries on the side.

780
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:03,960
I don't make much money,

781
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:05,360
but I'm getting by.

782
00:41:05,400 --> 00:41:06,280
Doing pretty well, actually.

783
00:41:08,480 --> 00:41:09,599
Even I can manage.

784
00:41:09,760 --> 00:41:11,679
And Old Qian's way more talented than me,

785
00:41:12,079 --> 00:41:12,679
with so much skill.

786
00:41:12,679 --> 00:41:13,760
So in the future,

787
00:41:14,440 --> 00:41:15,239
the sky's the limit for him.

788
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,639
Tu... Xiao Tu.

789
00:41:25,159 --> 00:41:26,519
Can I ask you a question?

790
00:41:27,440 --> 00:41:28,360
G-Go ahead.

791
00:41:29,079 --> 00:41:31,000
What body part fears the cold least?

792
00:41:34,440 --> 00:41:35,480
Right, you looked at me.

793
00:41:35,639 --> 00:41:36,440
You're smart.

794
00:41:36,519 --> 00:41:38,000
It's the eyes that don't fear the cold.

795
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:40,719
One Hundred Thousand Whys says

796
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:42,199
that the human eyeball

797
00:41:42,199 --> 00:41:43,360
is made of the conjunctiva,

798
00:41:43,440 --> 00:41:44,960
cornea, and sclera.

799
00:41:45,559 --> 00:41:47,360
These layers have all sorts of nerves,

800
00:41:47,440 --> 00:41:49,519
except for temperature receptors.

801
00:41:49,679 --> 00:41:51,880
That's why our eyes never feel the cold.

802
00:41:57,400 --> 00:41:58,119
Xiao Tu.

803
00:41:59,159 --> 00:41:59,960
I think

804
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:03,639
sometimes we should learn from our eyes.

805
00:42:04,760 --> 00:42:05,920
We shouldn't fear the cold either.

806
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:11,480
Cao Jun.

807
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:15,840
Are you always this carefree?

808
00:42:18,719 --> 00:42:20,559
Your wife walked out on you years ago.

809
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:22,719
Don't you resent her at all?

810
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:25,360
Why resent her?

811
00:42:25,760 --> 00:42:27,079
Look at the mess I've made of myself.

812
00:42:27,119 --> 00:42:28,079
As long as she's doing better than me,

813
00:42:28,079 --> 00:42:29,119
isn't that better than anything else?

814
00:42:29,480 --> 00:42:30,079
Right?

815
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:33,239
What do you think of me?

816
00:42:34,199 --> 00:42:34,920
You're pretty great.

817
00:42:37,920 --> 00:42:39,360
When you first came to the admin office,

818
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:41,199
you couldn't take your eyes off me.

819
00:42:41,639 --> 00:42:42,679
Don't think I didn't notice.

820
00:42:45,360 --> 00:42:46,360
N-No, that's not...

821
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:47,079
I... I...

822
00:42:47,119 --> 00:42:47,679
Xiao Tu...

823
00:42:47,719 --> 00:42:48,800
Do you like me?

824
00:42:54,079 --> 00:42:55,000
I do.

825
00:42:55,199 --> 00:42:55,800
No, no, wait...

826
00:42:55,840 --> 00:42:56,760
Tomorrow is Little New Year.

827
00:42:57,719 --> 00:42:58,639
Let's spend it together.

828
00:43:02,800 --> 00:43:03,440
Sure.

829
00:43:03,639 --> 00:43:04,239
Just say it...

830
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:04,920
Yes.

831
00:43:07,599 --> 00:43:08,280
Good.

832
00:43:20,519 --> 00:43:21,199
Cao Jun.

833
00:43:22,159 --> 00:43:23,639
I'll come to your place tomorrow night.

834
00:43:29,360 --> 00:43:30,079
All right.

835
00:44:06,039 --> 00:44:06,760
Give it to me.

836
00:44:07,119 --> 00:44:07,599
Zhao Haipeng.

837
00:44:11,159 --> 00:44:12,400
Why did you even come back?

838
00:44:13,760 --> 00:44:15,280
Nothing good happens when you're back.

839
00:44:15,880 --> 00:44:16,760
Tell me,

840
00:44:18,000 --> 00:44:20,199
when I found Ma Guowen cooking the books,

841
00:44:20,599 --> 00:44:22,039
if I hadn't exposed him...
